NAME
    jsc - compile explicitly described classic JavaScript modules

SYNOPSIS
    jsc <manifest.json> <output.js>

DESCRIPTION
    Compile a version-1 JSON module manifest into a classic JavaScript script
    that registers every declared module through JscRuntime.installBatch.

    jsc is a compiler. It does not embed, install or execute the independent
    JavaScript dynamic loader. The consumer loads dynamic-loader.lib.js first,
    then the compiled registration script. For a single-file distribution,
    an explicit separate packaging step can concatenate the loader and the
    compiler output.

    The launcher is an m bootstrap-integrated command. It uses the default
    m-managed nodejs runtime; it does not install nodejs implicitly.

OPERANDS
    manifest.json
        Readable JSON object with version 1 and modules array. Each module has
        id, relative file and deps array; optional format can only be classic.

    output.js
        Output file receiving one classic registration script.

SOURCE FORMAT
    Module files contain function-body JavaScript. At runtime each factory
    receives require, module and exports. Dependencies must be declared in
    the manifest. A module may set module.exports or exports.

    Static ESM import/export and import.meta syntax are not translated:
    incompatible sources are rejected. ESM projects use their separate
    compiler/loader path. Dynamic native import() is not managed by jsc.

OUTPUT
    Compilation verifies source syntax, module identifiers, manifest-tree
    containment and dependency graph completeness and acyclicity before
    writing output. Failed validation preserves any previous output file.

EXIT STATUS
    The launcher and its Node.js compiler have separate failure boundaries.
    A Node compiler exit status is propagated unchanged. The diagnostic
    jsc.<message-id> identifies the branch when numeric values overlap.

    Launcher (m fatal):
    1    Invalid command arguments.
    2    Compiler engine unavailable.
    3    Default m-managed nodejs runtime unavailable.
    4    Node command unavailable.

    Node compiler:
    0    Success.
    1    Invalid arguments.
    2    Manifest unreadable.
    3    No modules declared.
    4    Module source path cannot be resolved.
    5    Invalid classic JavaScript source syntax.
    6    Circular module dependency.
    7    Generated JavaScript invalid.
    8    Output write failure.
    9    Unexpected compiler failure.
    10   Invalid module identifier.
    11   Malformed manifest JSON.
    12   Unsupported manifest structure.
    13   Invalid module record.
    14   Duplicate module ID.
    15   Unsupported source format.
    16   Invalid source filename.
    17   Dependency list is not an array.
    18   Self-dependency.
    19   Duplicate declared dependency.
    20   Source resolves outside manifest tree.
    21   Module source unreadable.
    22   Missing graph dependency.

DIAGNOSTICS
    The m launcher uses localized log/fatal identities such as
    jsc.engine-unavailable and jsc.managed-node-unavailable. Successful
    invocation also records compilation-started at info, with debug/trace
    diagnostics for runtime resolution and child process completion.

    The Node engine executes in a distinct process without shell log/fatal.
    Compiler errors are emitted as [error] [jsc.<message-id>] diagnostics
    with contextual details. The launcher deliberately avoids duplicating
    these errors with another fatal message.

EXAMPLE
    jsc ./modules.json ./compiled.js

